+**`--clock` also reports that divergence, sampled.** `session_drift` is the
+distance right now between the session's projection (`anchor +
+monotonic_elapsed`) and a fresh read of the system clock, with a word for which
+side is ahead; `session_drift_ticks` is the same distance as an exact tick
+count. For a process that just started, this is small — the session has not had
+time to diverge from the clock it was anchored to. It grows with how long the
+process has been running and with how fast the oscillator and the wall clock's
+discipline disagree; it is not a claim about which one is closer to the truth.
